{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nLittle C loves number \u00ab3\u00bb very much. He loves all things about it.Now he is playing a game on a chessboard of size $$$n \\times m$$$. The cell in the $$$x$$$-th row and in the $$$y$$$-th column is called $$$(x,y)$$$. Initially, The chessboard is empty. Each time, he places two chessmen on two different empty cells, the Manhattan distance between which is exactly $$$3$$$. The Manhattan distance between two cells $$$(x_i,y_i)$$$ and $$$(x_j,y_j)$$$ is defined as $$$|x_i-x_j|+|y_i-y_j|$$$.He want to place as many chessmen as possible on the chessboard. Please help him find the maximum number of chessmen he can place.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 8 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\npublic class littleCloves3II {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc=new Scanner(System.in);\n       long n=sc.nextInt();\n       long m=sc.nextInt();\n        if(n<m) {\n            n = n + m;\n            m = n - m;\n            n = n - m;\n        }\n        int ans;\n        if(m==1)\n        {\n  